+
+# Serve post search and creation to assistants over MCP
+
+## Context
+
+Authors write with their own AI assistants and want them to search what the
+blog has published and to draft posts, without copying text between the two.
+The assistant is theirs, so the blog has to be reachable over MCP rather than
+grow a chatbot. We do not want a second implementation of search or of post
+creation, and we do not want to maintain JSON-RPC or MCP handling ourselves.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Two existing routes declare `agent` metadata in `routes/web.ts`:
+  `posts.search` and `posts.store`. The tools are derived from the routes'
+  own schemas, and a call re-enters the app as an HTTP request, so the
+  validation, the `auth` middleware and `PostPolicy` run as they do for a
+  browser. No other route is exposed.
+- The tools are named `posts_search` and `posts_store` through `toolName`.
+  Some assistants drop a tool whose name has a dot; the route names keep it.
+- `posts_search` is read-only because QUERY is a safe method; `posts_store`
+  carries no read-only hint, so an assistant asks its user first.
+- `@guren/plugin-mcp` serves the tools at `/mcp`, registered in `src/app.ts`.
+- Callers authenticate with the framework's API tokens, stored hashed in the
+  `api_tokens` table. A token belongs to one user and every call acts as that
+  user; its abilities (`tools:read`, `tool:posts_store`, `tools:*`) decide
+  which tools it reaches. Ops issue one with `bunx guren token:issue`.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A change to the post form's rules or to `PostPolicy` reaches assistants in
+  the same deploy, with nothing to keep in sync.
+- `PostController.store` has two responses to one action: the form gets its
+  redirect, and a caller sending `Accept: application/json` (which a tool call
+  does) gets `201` with `{ data: <post> }`, since a redirect tells an
+  assistant nothing about what it created. Any other JSON client of
+  `POST /posts` gets the same answer.
+- Rate limits are the plugin's defaults and are per process.
+- There is no page for users to create or revoke their own tokens yet, and
+  deleting a user deletes their tokens.
